+super-roast verdict: Should-fix (5 confirmed)
+mode: design        iteration: 1 of 3
+profile (assumed): herdr-graph is a Rust CLI plus a local Unix-socket daemon, shipped as a Herdr plugin (`publish = false`, v0.2.0) that keeps a Git-backed organization graph for human and agent collaborators on one developer's machine. No network exposure, no external users, no real money; state lives in a git repository with plan/undo, so rollback is cheap. The artifact under review is a security control (an approval gate for cross-agent instruction edits), so findings that touch the gate's own stated guarantee are weighed as correctness, while resilience, observability and cost findings are down-weighted.
