+## Confirmed findings
+- [Should-fix] §2.2 "The content must be valid UTF-8"; §2.4 diff detail; §4.1 verbatim render — Instruction content is validated only as UTF-8. Invisible or control characters (Unicode tag block U+E0000-E007F, zero-width, bidi overrides, ANSI escapes) pass validation, render as nothing in the approval diff, and are fed verbatim to every affected seat's model. The user can approve a change that differs from what the model receives.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Spec grep for utf, control, invisible, unicode, escape, ansi, sanitiz finds only UTF-8 checks (§1.4, §2.2, §4.1 placeholder). §3.5 residual list does not include it. https://embracethered.com/blog/posts/2024/hiding-and-finding-text-with-unicode-tags/ quotes Unicode TR51: "A completely tag-unaware implementation will display any sequence of tag characters as invisible", and notes LLMs interpret such text. Floor check: considered against the injection floor; not lifted to Blocking because §3.5 already accepts strictly stronger bypasses (direct socket calls) for an adversarial agent, so no capability is reached that the invoker could not already reach under the spec's own trust model. Fix first anyway: it defeats the review step through the sanctioned path.
+  fix-shape hint: At plan time reject (or escape visibly in the diff) Cf, Cc other than \n and \t, U+E0000-E007F, zero-width and bidi override code points, and ESC; add a test with a tag-block payload.
+
+- [Should-fix] Key decisions "Every plan commits only through `herdr-graph apply`"; §3.3 "the terminal `[y/n]` prompt for humans stays"; §3.5 residual vectors; §2.5 Undo — The tty `[y/n]` paths of `herdr-graph plan …` (shared by `rebind`) and interactive `herdr-graph undo` commit via `plan.apply`/`undo.apply` in tty mode without ever running `herdr-graph apply`, so the `Bash(herdr-graph apply:*)` ask rule never fires. An agent with a pty (`script -qc`, a Herdr pane) answers `y` itself. §3.5 does not list this second commit path, and the Key decisions sentence is false for it.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: src/cli/plan.rs:80-111 `plan_flow` under `Decision::Prompt` reads y/n and calls `plan.apply` with `mode:"tty"`. src/cli/undo.rs ~126 calls `undo.apply` with `mode:"tty"`. src/plan/commands.rs:239 `"tty" if caller.tty => ConfirmMode::Tty`. src/daemon/client.rs:89 sets `tty` from `stdin().is_terminal()`. §3.5 lists prompt-skipping modes, `sh -c`/`env`/alias rewraps, socket calls, settings edits, direct git commits; not this path. Refute seat argued it is within the cooperative contract; it did not dispute the premise that the Key decisions sentence and §3.5 are inaccurate.
+  fix-shape hint: Either add the tty `plan`/`rebind`/`undo` commit path to §3.5 and correct the Key decisions wording, or make the tty prompt refuse (print the relay hint) when the caller is a harness seat.
+
+- [Should-fix] §4.1 order ("later section wins") with §4.4 "Output is capped at HOOK_RENDER_CAP = 9000 bytes, cut at a line boundary" — Truncation keeps a prefix and drops the tail, and §4.1 puts seat rules and seat AGENTS.md last as the winning layer. An oversized stack silently drops exactly the highest-precedence seat parts and keeps the general rules they override. Recovery depends on the agent obeying the marker, the dependency Main challenges says to remove. No size budget, plan-time warning or doctor check exists.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: §4.1 steps 1-6 global → teamspace → templates → sections → seat rules → seat AGENTS.md; header "on conflict the later section wins". §4.4 cut at a line boundary plus marker. Main challenges: "without depending on the agent obeying a 'run /seat' prompt". https://code.claude.com/docs/en/hooks: additionalContext and plain stdout "are capped at 10,000 characters", overflow saved to a file with a 2,000-character preview, "Claude Code doesn't ask Claude to read the file", so a hard cap is real and the drop order is the defect. A single approved global rules edit grows every seat's render.
+  fix-shape hint: Truncate from the general end (or reserve budget for steps 5-6), and emit a plan-time warning when an edit pushes any affected seat's render past the cap.
+
+- [Should-fix] §4.1 steps 3 and 6 with "later section wins"; §1.5 "update their instance's summarizer template through plan template edit" — Seats hydrated from inline-template members (including the shipped summarizer) carry a frozen seeded copy of the member AGENTS.md as seat AGENTS.md. The render places it last, so it wins over a `plan template edit` and duplicates the text. The §1.5 migration note never tells users to also clear or set the seat AGENTS.md, so a migrated summarizer keeps calling the removed `content write`.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: src/templates/kinds.rs:432-436 `create_member_seat` seeds `<seat>/AGENTS.md` when `member.seat_template.is_none()`. templates/system-summarizer/template.toml: summarizer member has no `seat_template`. templates/system-summarizer/members/summarizer/AGENTS.md:26 contains `herdr-graph content write`. `bound_paths` (src/bootstrap/mod.rs ~160-180) renders members/<slug>/AGENTS.md at step 3 and the seat copy at step 6. Problem statement: "without stranding … the summarizer pipeline"; §1.5 stub exits 2.
+  fix-shape hint: Extend the CHANGELOG/§1.5 note to also run `plan instructions clear seat <summarizer> AGENTS.md` (or set it), and have the leaf decide whether inline seeding should be dropped or deduplicated in the render.
+
+- [Should-fix] §2.1 "`<name>` matches `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*`" vs §4.1 "rules/*.md (by file name)"; Key abstractions InstructionSource predicate — §2.1 restricts editable rule names to a regex while §4.1 renders every `rules/*.md` and today's `markdown_in` loads any `.md`. A pre-existing nonconforming name (e.g. `rules/Code-Style.md`) is either rendered but uneditable and unclearable through any plan, or silently demoted to `data`. The spec picks neither and specifies no migration or doctor check.
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: src/bootstrap/mod.rs:99-112 `markdown_in` lists every file ending in `.md` with no name filter. §2.1 calls the file set "closed". §1 requirement: "without stranding any instruction source" and "Every instruction file outside templates becomes editable". §5/§6 list migration only for the summarizer template and no doctor check for rule names. Refute seat confirmed at Nit (edge case, hand-committed rename is a workaround); kept at Should-fix because the fix is one sentence and the spec must choose glob vs regex before the leaf implements both the renderer and the predicate.
+  fix-shape hint: One sentence deciding whether the renderer and `data` predicate use the §2.1 regex or the `.md` glob, with `set`/`clear` accepting whatever the renderer accepts, plus a doctor warning (or migration note) for nonconforming or nested files.
