+## Escalations (need human)
+- §3.2 "if it cannot confirm, the file is still written" — UNVERIFIED external: whether a malformed or unsupported Codex `.rules` file aborts Codex startup or is ignored is not documented (https://developers.openai.com/codex/rules says only that match/not_match examples are validated at load). If it aborts, the blast radius of an unconfirmed write is every Codex session on the machine. Cheapest check: put a malformed file in an isolated `CODEX_HOME/rules/` and run `codex`; if startup fails, setup must not write an unconfirmed file.
+- §4.4 "checked by the implementing leaf, which first looks up Claude's documented limit" — material dissent on the Codex hook-output limit: the reproduce seat fetched https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/hooks, which says "By default, Codex limits each model-visible hook-output message to roughly 2,500 tokens" with oversized output replaced by a head-and-tail preview (configurable via `additionalContextLimit`), so a 9000-byte render can be cut by Codex itself without herdr-graph's marker; the refute and ground seats searched, found no Codex limit, and rejected on "unknown, and the spec flags the cap as an assumption". The seat evidence does not settle whether 9000 bytes exceeds 2,500 tokens for typical instruction text or whether the trailing marker survives the preview. Needs a human to confirm the Codex figure and, if real, add a Codex-specific lookup and a lower per-harness cap to §4.4.
