+- §3.2 "if it cannot confirm, the file is still written" — §3.2 has setup write the Codex rules file even when its syntax cannot be confirmed, but the spec never considers what a malformed or unsupported `.rules` file does to Codex startup. If Codex refuses to load or start, the blast radius is every Codex session on the machine, not only the gate. (external-unverified)
